<!-- ===== [7] FAQ ===== -->
<section id="faq" class="mb-16">
 <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
  <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl p-8 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
   <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-8 text-center">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
   <div class="space-y-6 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
     <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">What is the difference between a factory audit, supplier verification, and pre-shipment inspection?</h3>
     <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Supplier verification is desk research: business license check, ISO cert verification, financial background: cost $100-200. Factory audit is on-site: walkthrough, equipment inspection, live tests, red flag hunting: cost $300-800. Pre-shipment inspection (PSI) is per-order: inspecting finished goods before they leave the factory at 80-100% production completion: cost $200-350. A first-time supplier requires all three; repeat suppliers need only PSI on each order.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
     <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">Can I do a factory audit remotely, or do I need to fly to China?</h3>
     <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Remote video audits catch documentation issues but rarely catch physical staging (empty aging rooms, borrowed SMT lines, brokered facilities). For first-time suppliers or orders above $50,000, an in-person audit is worth the flight. For subsequent visits to a verified supplier, a video walk-through led by the same QC manager can substitute at 40-50% of on-site cost.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
     <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">How long does an on-site factory audit take for a charger or power bank supplier?</h3>
     <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Half a day (3-4 hours) for a focused audit covering the 25 checkpoints in this article. A full-day audit adds financial due diligence, environmental compliance review, and social audit elements: 7-8 hours total. Most buyers underinvest. A 2-hour audit is a photo op, not verification. Budget the full 4 hours to reach Zones 4-6 (aging, QC lab, warehouse) where verification value peaks.</p>
    </div>
    
    
    <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
     <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">How much does a professional factory audit cost in Shenzhen (SGS/Bureau Veritas/QIMA)?</h3>
     <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">$300-600 per auditor-day in Shenzhen for a single-auditor day. Multi-day comprehensive audits run $1,000-2,500. QIMA is typically the most cost-effective for a first audit at ~$309 flat. SGS $350-550/day. Bureau Veritas $350-550/day. Intertek $400-600/day. All four publish English-language reports within 5-7 business days. Bring your own audit priorities. Third parties run a generic checklist unless you specify what matters.</p>
    </div>
    
    <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
     <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">What MOQ and payment terms should I expect from a WOWOHCOOL factory audit visit?</h3>
     <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">WOWOHCOOL MOQ is 500 units for ODM, 3,000 units for full OEM with logo + color + packaging + certification. Payment: 30% deposit + 70% before shipment via T/T for first order; 30/70 or net-30 after 3 orders; L/C available above $50,000. Factory visits include a 30-minute walkthrough with the QC manager plus a live nail test / thermal / Hi-Pot demonstration at no cost. Request a visit at wowohcool.com/contact/.</p>
    </div>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
</section>

